      "statusChangeID": "60996cb58e09cb3bd3ae96e0",
      "statusChangeNewStatus": "tracked",
      "value": "@{5c1475afb7ce126e9e0e3a39|full_name}: What do you think about this phrasing instead:\nThis node is used in Manual Sync mode to flag the variables on the target UdonBehaviour for Serialization during the next Network Tick, which does not happen every frame. Example: you have a synced float variable called 'sliderValue'. When a UISlider's value changes, you trigger RequestSerialization, which triggers an OnPreSerialization event during the next Network Tick. When this event triggers, you set 'sliderValue' from the current value of the slider, and everyone in the instance will receive this new value.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-05-08T23:39:18.112Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "The documentation states:\n> This node works will with the OnPreSerialization Event node. You trigger \"RequestSerialization\" and then the OnPreSerialization event will trigger during the next Network Tick.\nApart from the \"will\" typo, this has two potential areas of concern.\n1. If you only invoke RequestSerialization from OnPreSerialization, when does serialization get triggered?\n2. When I tried on prior builds, RequestSerialization did not queue up a second serialization when invoked in OnPreSerialization (the current serialization would have been requested elsewhere). OnPostSerialization did work, however.",
